    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44497" root="&#xA;                        ودع&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            3
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَادَعَهُ</span></b> 
                        , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوَادَعَةٌ</span>, and subst. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِدَاعٌ</span>, <i>He
made peace</i> or <i>reconciled himself, with him:</i>
(Msb:) [the inf. n.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوَادَعَةٌ</span> is <i>syn. with</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُصَالَحَةٌ</span>
because it is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَارَكَةٌ</span> [<i>a mutual leaving,</i> or <i>leaving
unmolested</i>]. (Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوَادَعَةٌ</span> is also syn.
with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرْكٌ</span>; as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَعَةٌ</span></b> : (TA:) so that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَادَعَهُ</span>
signifies <i>He left him:</i> but more correctly, <i>he
left him, being left by him;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَارَكَهُ</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالَاهُ</span>; and this is the primary meaning.

